Here is a full audit of every user-facing control in Settings, plus in-flow controls that duplicate or shadow settings. Scores are **1–5** for how important it is that users can change this vs. a fixed default.

**Score key:** 5 = essential control · 4 = important for some users · 3 = power user · 2 = low value · 1 = should be fixed/hidden

---

## General

| Tab | Section | Name | Action | Interaction | Score | Reason |
|-----|---------|------|--------|-------------|-------|--------|
| General | Appearance | Theme (System / Dark / Light) | Sets app colour scheme | Pick option → **Save** | 1 | Cosmetic; System default is fine for most.  |
| General | Keyboard shortcuts | Scribe keyboard shortcut | Shows global hotkey to open Scribe | **Read-only** display | 1 | Already fixed (`Cmd/Ctrl+Shift+L`). Display-only is correct — editable global hotkeys are a support nightmare. |
| General | Keyboard shortcuts | Dictate keyboard shortcut | Shows Dictate activation pattern | **Read-only** display | 1 | Fixed double-tap modifier behaviour. No reason to expose editing. |
| General | Scribe | Default save folder | Where transcripts, dictate history, failures are saved | Path picker → **Save** | 5 | Users must control output location (Documents vs project folder vs cloud sync path). |
| General | Scribe | Save transcripts as Markdown | Also writes `.md` files alongside JSONL history | Toggle → **Save** | 3 | Power-user / workflow choice. Default OFF is sensible; many users never need this. |
| General | Scribe | Keep audio after transcription | Retains WAV after successful Scribe transcription | Toggle → **Save** | 3 | Important for re-transcription, archival, legal use. Default OFF is right; option should stay somewhere. |
| General | Scribe | Open transcripts with | App used to open `.md` files (when markdown export on) | Path picker → **Save** | 3 | Only matters if markdown export is on. Could be inferred from OS default. |
| General | Scribe speaker capture | Speaker capture device name *(macOS only)* | Names the Multi-Output / BlackHole device for loopback | Text field → **Save** | 5 *(mac)* / N/A *(Win)* | Required for macOS speaker capture to work at all. Cannot be predetermined. |
| General | Scribe speaker capture | Input label | Prefix for mic lines in dual-source transcripts (default `in:`) | Text field → **Save** | 1 | `in:` / `out:` defaults work for 95% of users. Custom labels are niche. |
| General | Scribe speaker capture | Output label | Prefix for speaker lines (default `out:`) | Text field → **Save** | 1 | Same as input label — low value to expose. |
| General | Scribe speaker capture | Capture speaker by default | Pre-enables speaker capture when Scribe opens | Toggle → **Save** | 3 | Meeting-heavy users want this on; solo note-takers don't. Per-session toggle also exists (see below). |
| General | Dictate | Press Enter after dictate | Sends Enter keystroke after paste | Toggle → **Save** | 3 | Messaging/search apps need it; word processors don't. Real workflow split. |
| General | *(footer)* | Save | Persists all General changes in one batch | Button click | — | Batch save adds friction; most toggles elsewhere auto-save. |

**Hidden config (no UI):** `preferred_input_device` is loaded/saved with General but has **no field** — mic choice lives in the TitleBar recording popover instead. `dictate_auto_paste` defaults ON with **no UI** (paste always attempted when Accessibility granted).

